      "side": 1,
      "message": "Look at the doc for `Looper#prepare` :\n\n      * Be sure to call {@link #loop()} after calling this method\n\nYou can\u0027t ignore this. This will blow up in your face.\n\nLooper fully assumes it is running the loop. Many functions in the framework assume the looper is running the loop, including functions that just do things differently if a looper is currently prepared. E.g., they could post something assuming the looper is running, and you won\u0027t run that code, so doing this will break arbitrary system server functions in creative ways and it will be very hard to debug.\n\nIf you *must* use a looper you must have a thread that is actually running the loop. The system server has a number of existing threads that are ready for you to do this. BackgroundThread is typically a good choice for the kind of usage you have.",
